ughter Caroline  Caroline's sister Kate also served as  did their husbands their brothers-in-law  their  father Jerry both grandfathers and  ancestors long before them seven  generations seven generations unbroken  line an unbroken commitment forged at  the US Military Academy at West Point in  New York and I think some people are  willing to step up to that that  challenge and I call and others are not  on this campus the sisters learned a  craft that Outsiders don't always  understand the first question is that I  dread getting is have you killed anyone  have you shot anyone or it's just the  wrong question to ask people have asked  most of you as Americans don't know them  many of you don't know anyone who knows  any in one of them last October White  House chief of staff John Kelly called  out the public's isolation from the  troops general Kelly's son was killed in  Afghanistan they are the very best of  these country producers and they  volunteer to protect our country when  there's nothing in our country anymore  it seems to suggest that self service to  the nation is not only appropriate but  required you can't make people  understand what you do Jerry says  Kelly's remarks were necessary you can  only hope that they will become you know  maybe more aware I get a lot of people  who come up to me and in the veterans  day and say you know thank you for  serving and so on and so forth I get  others that don't even know that it's  Veterans Day it's hard to be aware  because civilians may never meet a  military family they move from base to  base as Claire did growing up  when Jerry and I got married that was my  53rd address we had lived in hotel rooms  we had lived in a water tower at one  time she passed on the lifestyle to her  daughter Kate who was moved 17 times in  18 years I've spent every day of my  adult life serving the military either  as a spouse or as a military officer and  many days both why is it important that  people should understand the servi